    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1237">

                <pb facs="1218" n="932" xml:id="pg932"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 867.48/312</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-07T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 7, 1916, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2814. Department’s 2784, June 24, 5 p. m. Again inform Turkish Government of the
                    great sympathy which the citizens of the United States feel for the destitute in
                    Syria, and add that a refusal of the Turkish Government to give friendly
                    consideration to this Government’s suggestion regarding relief supplies for
                    Syria will not be understood in this country and might seriously affect in the
                    future the sentiments here toward the Turkish Government and Turkish people.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
